      "writtenOn": "2020-11-18T18:47:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On Grunt, is the EN_PP5000 controlled by EC? or some discrete circuitry?\n\nIn many other boards, the EN_PP5000 is controlled by EC. The PD task is actually one of the consumers of the PP5000 rails. We can define the CONFIG_POWER_PP5000_CONTROL and add the dependency in the board-special pd_set_power_supply_ready(). So as long as the PD is sourcing power, the PP5000 rail won\u0027t be turned off, i.e. VBUS keeping high.",
      "parentUuid": "2db07e28_d33c7254",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "0fc1c277b2a459a4500b8315d50e015157e76162",
